Negated conjunction of errors.Is / errors.As over a dynamic Begin (memory + filerepo):
if !errors.Is(err, retry.ErrBusy) && !errors.As(err, &te) { return err }; return fmt.Errorf("tx: store busy: %w", err).
Go semantics: memory.ErrClosed and filerepo's lock errors bare; retry.ErrBusy and *retry.TimeoutError ONLY behind
"tx: store busy: %w"; Rollback's errors (repo.ErrTxDone via memTx, os.Remove errors via fileTx) bare.
Recorded: the early return is filtered exactly (no bare ErrBusy / *TimeoutError), but the fall-through keeps
everything: sentinel memory.ErrClosed is also listed behind "tx: store busy: %w". Not flagged: the wrap is reached
from the true edge of either check and neither dominates it, so by the dominance rule of plan S07 no guard applies
there - a documented, sound over-approximation (the same shape in retry.Do puts non-transient errors behind
"%w after %d attempts: %w"). Nothing may be missing.
-- args --
